  "captions": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 1.32,
      "text": "Two papers said this:"
    },
    {
      "start": 1.07,
      "end": 5.062,
      "text": "a dispute about how somebody died goes\nto a private arbitrator."
    },
    {
      "start": 5.112,
      "end": 8.288,
      "text": "A dispute about an unpaid bill stays\nin a courthouse."
    },
    {
      "start": 9.838,
      "end": 13.839,
      "text": "The case is Marmet Health Care Center\nagainst Clayton Brown,"
    },
    {
      "start": 13.589,
      "end": 18.215,
      "text": "decided by the Supreme Court of the United States\non February 21, 2012."
    },
    {
      "start": 18.265,
      "end": 21.444,
      "text": "It is five pages long, and it is per curiam —"
    },
    {
      "start": 21.194,
      "end": 26.735,
      "text": "an opinion issued by the Court with no author's\nname on it and no vote reported."
    },
    {
      "start": 26.785,
      "end": 28.057,
      "text": "Five pages."
    },
    {
      "start": 28.107,
      "end": 30.417,
      "text": "Almost everything a person would want"
    },
    {
      "start": 30.167,
      "end": 33.001,
      "text": "to know about these three families is not in them."
    },
    {
      "start": 34.551,
      "end": 38.397,
      "text": "This litigation involves three negligence suits\nagainst nursing homes"
    },
    {
      "start": 38.147,
      "end": 42.253,
      "text": "in West Virginia. That is the opinion's own first\nline of fact."
    },
    {
      "start": 42.303,
      "end": 46.686,
      "text": "The suits were brought by Clayton Brown, Jeffrey\nTaylor, and Sharon Marchio."
    },
    {
      "start": 46.736,
      "end": 50.444,
      "text": "Brown sued Marmet Health Care Center.\nSo did Taylor."
    },
    {
      "start": 50.494,
      "end": 53.066,
      "text": "Marchio sued a nursing home in Clarksburg."
    },
    {
      "start": 53.116,
      "end": 56.203,
      "text": "In the Supreme Court's caption it has two names —"
    },
    {
      "start": 55.953,
      "end": 59.292,
      "text": "Clarksburg Nursing Home and Rehabilitation Center,"
    },
    {
      "start": 59.042,
      "end": 62.329,
      "text": "doing business as Clarksburg Continuous Care\nCenter."
    },
    {
      "start": 62.379,
      "end": 67.758,
      "text": "She sued as executrix of the estate of Pauline\nVirginia Willett. Three plaintiffs."
    },
    {
      "start": 67.808,
      "end": 73.952,
      "text": "Two nursing homes. One state. The first order came\non August 25, 2009."
    },
    {
      "start": 74.002,
      "end": 77.642,
      "text": "The Circuit Court of Kanawha County dismissed\nClayton Brown's suit."
    },
    {
      "start": 77.692,
      "end": 83.043,
      "text": "Brown had argued that the arbitration clause\nwas unenforceable on two grounds —"
    },
    {
      "start": 82.793,
      "end": 87.202,
      "text": "that it violated section 15(c) of the state's\nNursing Home Act,"
    },
    {
      "start": 86.952,
      "end": 90.62,
      "text": "and that it was an unconscionable contract\nof adhesion."
    },
    {
      "start": 90.67,
      "end": 92.465,
      "text": "The circuit court disagreed,"
    },
    {
      "start": 92.215,
      "end": 95.184,
      "text": "and ruled that under the admission agreement\nsigned"
    },
    {
      "start": 94.934,
      "end": 98.861,
      "text": "with the nursing home he was required to arbitrate\nall of his claims."
    },
    {
      "start": 98.911,
      "end": 104.569,
      "text": "That order is one paragraph long. One paragraph."
    },
    {
      "start": 104.619,
      "end": 106.9,
      "text": "Its stated basis is a single clause:"
    },
    {
      "start": 106.65,
      "end": 110.77,
      "text": "the court determined that Brown was required\nto arbitrate his claims"
    },
    {
      "start": 110.52,
      "end": 115.364,
      "text": "after hearing argument of counsel, reviewing\nthe respective briefs and the record."
    },
    {
      "start": 115.414,
      "end": 120.862,
      "text": "No findings. No analysis. That paragraph comes\nback at the end of this story."
    },
    {
      "start": 120.912,
      "end": 124.134,
      "text": "Five weeks later, the same court did the same\nthing."
    },
    {
      "start": 124.184,
      "end": 127.27,
      "text": "The second order came on September 29, 2009,"
    },
    {
      "start": 127.02,
      "end": 130.85,
      "text": "and it dismissed Jeffrey Taylor's suit\nagainst owners,"
    },
    {
      "start": 130.6,
      "end": 134.001,
      "text": "operators and employees of the same nursing home."
    },
    {
      "start": 134.051,
      "end": 136.484,
      "text": "Taylor had made the same two arguments."
    },
    {
      "start": 136.534,
      "end": 140.896,
      "text": "The circuit court concluded\nthat under the admission agreement he was required"
    },
    {
      "start": 140.646,
      "end": 144.261,
      "text": "to arbitrate all of the claims asserted\nagainst the nursing home."
    },
    {
      "start": 144.311,
      "end": 148.39,
      "text": "Both plaintiffs appealed. The third order went\nthe other way."
    },
    {
      "start": 148.44,
      "end": 149.65,
      "text": "On June 2, 2010,"
    },
    {
      "start": 149.4,
      "end": 154.477,
      "text": "the Circuit Court of Harrison County refused\nto dismiss Sharon Marchio's suit"
    },
    {
      "start": 154.227,
      "end": 156.585,
      "text": "and refused to compel arbitration."
    },
    {
      "start": 156.635,
      "end": 158.948,
      "text": "Instead it certified a question upward,"
    },
    {
      "start": 158.698,
      "end": 163.276,
      "text": "because Marchio had argued that her clause\nwas unenforceable under the same section"
    },
    {
      "start": 163.026,
      "end": 164.501,
      "text": "of the Nursing Home Act."
    },
    {
      "start": 164.551,
      "end": 169.027,
      "text": "The question was whether that section\nwas preempted by the Federal Arbitration Act."
    },
    {
      "start": 169.077,
      "end": 173.599,
      "text": "Two dismissals and one question, all travelling\nto the state's highest court."
    },
    {
      "start": 173.649,
      "end": 175.942,
      "text": "Now the part where the record stops."
    },
    {
      "start": 175.992,
      "end": 179.659,
      "text": "Here is everything the Supreme Court's opinion\ntells you about what happened"
    },
    {
      "start": 179.409,
      "end": 182.533,
      "text": "to these three patients. It is two sentences."
    },
    {
      "start": 182.583,
      "end": 183.589,
      "text": "In each case,"
    },
    {
      "start": 183.339,
      "end": 184.482,
      "text": "a family member"
    },
    {
      "start": 184.232,
      "end": 188.543,
      "text": "of a patient requiring extensive nursing care\nhad signed an agreement"
    },
    {
      "start": 188.293,
      "end": 191.099,
      "text": "with a nursing home on behalf of the patient."
    },
    {
      "start": 191.149,
      "end": 192.995,
      "text": "In each of the three cases,"
    },
    {
      "start": 192.745,
      "end": 197.51,
      "text": "a family member of a patient who had died sued\nthe nursing home in state court,"
    },
    {
      "start": 197.26,
      "end": 201.43,
      "text": "alleging that negligence caused injuries or harm\nresulting in death."
    },
    {
      "start": 201.48,
      "end": 205.813,
      "text": "That is the whole account. No ages. No conditions."
    },
    {
      "start": 205.863,
      "end": 208.481,
      "text": "No dates of admission, no dates of death."
    },
    {
      "start": 208.531,
      "end": 210.318,
      "text": "No description of the care,"
    },
    {
      "start": 210.068,
      "end": 213.425,
      "text": "and no description of what the negligence was said\nto be."
    },
    {
      "start": 213.475,
      "end": 217.872,
      "text": "Pauline Virginia Willett is the only patient named\nanywhere in the opinion,"
    },
    {
      "start": 217.622,
      "end": 223.034,
      "text": "and she is named only in the caption of Marchio's\ncase. Brown's patient is unnamed."
    },
    {
      "start": 223.084,
      "end": 228.696,
      "text": "So is Taylor's. The signature is described twice,\nin the same four words."
    },
    {
      "start": 228.746,
      "end": 232.361,
      "text": "A family member. The opinion never says which."
    },
    {
      "start": 232.411,
      "end": 236.591,
      "text": "It never says whether the person who signed\nis the person who later sued,"
    },
    {
      "start": 236.341,
      "end": 239.581,
      "text": "and it never says what either of them\nwas to the patient."
    },
    {
      "start": 239.631,
      "end": 242.946,
      "text": "A five-page per curiam opinion is not a narrative."
    },
    {
      "start": 242.996,
      "end": 246.172,
      "text": "What the record does describe closely\nis the paper."
    },
    {
      "start": 246.222,
      "end": 249.419,
      "text": "The relevant parts of the agreements in Brown's\ncase"
    },
    {
      "start": 249.169,
      "end": 251.255,
      "text": "and Taylor's case were identical."
    },
    {
      "start": 251.305,
      "end": 255.644,
      "text": "Both contained a clause requiring the parties\nto arbitrate all disputes,"
    },
    {
      "start": 255.394,
      "end": 259.171,
      "text": "other than claims to collect late payments owed\nby the patient."
    },
    {
      "start": 259.221,
      "end": 263.765,
      "text": "So which dispute did the paper leave\nin a courthouse? Not the death."
    },
    {
      "start": 263.815,
      "end": 270.077,
      "text": "The money. There was a second provision\nin those two contracts."
    },
    {
      "start": 270.127,
      "end": 274.511,
      "text": "The party filing the arbitration is responsible\nfor paying a filing fee,"
    },
    {
      "start": 274.261,
      "end": 279.201,
      "text": "in accordance with the Rules of the American\nArbitration Association fee schedules."
    },
    {
      "start": 279.251,
      "end": 284.677,
      "text": "Whoever starts the proceeding pays to start it.\nThe opinion states no dollar figure."
    },
    {
      "start": 284.727,
      "end": 287.02,
      "text": "Marchio's paper was not that paper."
    },
    {
      "start": 287.07,
      "end": 291.857,
      "text": "The agreement in Marchio's case also included\na clause requiring arbitration,"
    },
    {
      "start": 291.607,
      "end": 295.139,
      "text": "but it made no exceptions to the arbitration\nrequirement"
    },
    {
      "start": 294.889,
      "end": 299.369,
      "text": "and it did not mention filing fees.\nNo carve-out for late payments."
    },
    {
      "start": 299.419,
      "end": 304.402,
      "text": "Nothing about who pays to file. Three families.\nTwo documents."
    },
    {
      "start": 304.452,
      "end": 307.906,
      "text": "The state law they were all pointing at was one\nsentence."
    },
    {
      "start": 307.956,
      "end": 313.217,
      "text": "Section 15(c) of the West Virginia Nursing Home\nAct, as it stood in 1997:"
    },
    {
      "start": 312.967,
      "end": 318.157,
      "text": "any waiver by a resident or his or her legal\nrepresentative of the right"
    },
    {
      "start": 317.907,
      "end": 322.973,
      "text": "to commence an action under this section,\nwhether oral or in writing,"
    },
    {
      "start": 322.723,
      "end": 326.457,
      "text": "shall be null and void as contrary to public\npolicy."
    },
    {
      "start": 326.507,
      "end": 330.493,
      "text": "A waiver of the right to commence an action. Null\nand void."
    },
    {
      "start": 330.543,
      "end": 335.019,
      "text": "West Virginia's legislature had put\nthat in the statute books in 1997."
    },
    {
      "start": 335.069,
      "end": 340.657,
      "text": "Whether it survived contact with a federal statute\npassed in 1925 was now a question"
    },
    {
      "start": 340.407,
      "end": 342.564,
      "text": "for the state's highest court."
    },
    {
      "start": 344.114,
      "end": 345.374,
      "text": "On June 29, 2011,"
    },
    {
      "start": 345.124,
      "end": 349.89,
      "text": "West Virginia's Supreme Court of Appeals decided\nall three cases together."
    },
    {
      "start": 349.94,
      "end": 353.674,
      "text": "It consolidated Brown's and Taylor's appeals\nwith Marchio's,"
    },
    {
      "start": 353.424,
      "end": 356.041,
      "text": "which was before the court on other issues."
    },
    {
      "start": 356.091,
      "end": 359.648,
      "text": "The court's own later description of what it\nproduced:"
    },
    {
      "start": 359.398,
      "end": 364.118,
      "text": "an extensive opinion with three holdings. Lawyers\ncall it Brown One."
    },
    {
      "start": 364.168,
      "end": 366.601,
      "text": "The first holding went against the patients."
    },
    {
      "start": 366.651,
      "end": 370.273,
      "text": "The state court took its own legislature's waiver\nban and held"
    },
    {
      "start": 370.023,
      "end": 372.752,
      "text": "that the Federal Arbitration Act preempted it."
    },
    {
      "start": 372.802,
      "end": 375.978,
      "text": "The reasoning was a rule the court stated\nfor itself."
    },
    {
      "start": 376.028,
      "end": 377.642,
      "text": "A state statute, rule,"
    },
    {
      "start": 377.392,
      "end": 381.448,
      "text": "or common-law doctrine which targets arbitration\nprovisions"
    },
    {
      "start": 381.198,
      "end": 383.17,
      "text": "for disfavored treatment,"
    },
    {
      "start": 382.92,
      "end": 387.626,
      "text": "and which is not usually applied to other types\nof contract provisions,"
    },
    {
      "start": 387.376,
      "end": 392.156,
      "text": "stands as an obstacle to the accomplishment\nand execution of the purposes"
    },
    {
      "start": 391.906,
      "end": 396.201,
      "text": "and objectives of the Federal Arbitration Act,\nand is preempted."
    },
    {
      "start": 396.251,
      "end": 400.377,
      "text": "That is the rule it wrote. Then it applied\nthat rule to Charleston."
    },
    {
      "start": 400.427,
      "end": 405.966,
      "text": "To the extent that section 15(c) attempts\nto nullify and void any arbitration clause"
    },
    {
      "start": 405.716,
      "end": 411.129,
      "text": "in a written contract which evidences\na transaction affecting interstate commerce,"
    },
    {
      "start": 410.879,
      "end": 414.286,
      "text": "between a nursing home and a nursing home resident"
    },
    {
      "start": 414.036,
      "end": 418.371,
      "text": "or the resident's legal representative,\nthe statute is preempted."
    },
    {
      "start": 418.421,
      "end": 423.083,
      "text": "The picture of a state court simply defying\nWashington does not survive that."
    },
    {
      "start": 423.133,
      "end": 426.494,
      "text": "On the statute, West Virginia agreed\nwith the nursing homes."
    },
    {
      "start": 426.544,
      "end": 430.927,
      "text": "Nobody appealed that holding, and the court\nwould later note that nobody had."
    },
    {
      "start": 430.977,
      "end": 433.688,
      "text": "The second holding is the one that travelled."
    },
    {
      "start": 433.738,
      "end": 436.211,
      "text": "It is Syllabus Point 21, and it reads:"
    },
    {
      "start": 435.961,
      "end": 439.419,
      "text": "Congress did not intend for arbitration\nagreements,"
    },
    {
      "start": 439.169,
      "end": 444.029,
      "text": "adopted prior to an occurrence of negligence\nthat results in a personal injury"
    },
    {
      "start": 443.779,
      "end": 445.145,
      "text": "or wrongful death,"
    },
    {
      "start": 444.895,
      "end": 449.811,
      "text": "and which require questions about the negligence\nbe submitted to arbitration,"
    },
    {
      "start": 449.561,
      "end": 455.719,
      "text": "to be governed by the Federal Arbitration Act.\nThe load is on one word. Prior."
    },
    {
      "start": 455.769,
      "end": 459.663,
      "text": "Prior to what? The court's argument\nwas about sequence."
    },
    {
      "start": 459.713,
      "end": 464.189,
      "text": "A commercial contract that goes wrong produces\na dispute about the contract."
    },
    {
      "start": 464.239,
      "end": 466.534,
      "text": "A nursing home admission agreement"
    },
    {
      "start": 466.284,
      "end": 470.642,
      "text": "that goes wrong produces something else entirely —\nan injury, a death —"
    },
    {
      "start": 470.392,
      "end": 474.413,
      "text": "and the paper routing that dispute\nto an arbitrator was signed"
    },
    {
      "start": 474.163,
      "end": 475.96,
      "text": "before the injury existed."
    },
    {
      "start": 476.01,
      "end": 479.929,
      "text": "From that the court drew the public policy\nthat gave the case its shape."
    },
    {
      "start": 479.979,
      "end": 483.34,
      "text": "Its own sentence, quoted back to it the next year\nin Washington."
    },
    {
      "start": 483.39,
      "end": 486.745,
      "text": "As a matter of public policy under West Virginia\nlaw,"
    },
    {
      "start": 486.495,
      "end": 491.053,
      "text": "an arbitration clause in a nursing home admission\nagreement adopted prior"
    },
    {
      "start": 490.803,
      "end": 495.857,
      "text": "to an occurrence of negligence that results\nin a personal injury or wrongful death,"
    },
    {
      "start": 495.607,
      "end": 500.637,
      "text": "shall not be enforced to compel arbitration\nof a dispute concerning the negligence."
    },
    {
      "start": 500.687,
      "end": 504.162,
      "text": "Not this clause. Not these three clauses."
    },
    {
      "start": 504.212,
      "end": 508.502,
      "text": "Any such clause, in any nursing home admission\nagreement in the state."
    },
    {
      "start": 508.552,
      "end": 511.681,
      "text": "The third holding was about these particular\npapers."
    },
    {
      "start": 511.731,
      "end": 513.612,
      "text": "In two of the three cases,"
    },
    {
      "start": 513.362,
      "end": 519.11,
      "text": "the court ruled that the arbitration clauses\nwere unconscionable and unenforceable —"
    },
    {
      "start": 518.86,
      "end": 520.48,
      "text": "Brown's and Taylor's."
    },
    {
      "start": 520.53,
      "end": 522.149,
      "text": "In the third, Marchio's,"
    },
    {
      "start": 521.899,
      "end": 524.562,
      "text": "it answered the certified question and held"
    },
    {
      "start": 524.312,
      "end": 528.32,
      "text": "that the Nursing Home Act could not be relied upon\nto bar enforcement"
    },
    {
      "start": 528.07,
      "end": 531.183,
      "text": "of an arbitration clause in a nursing home\ncontract."
    },
    {
      "start": 531.233,
      "end": 533.619,
      "text": "So the court had built two separate doors."
    },
    {
      "start": 533.669,
      "end": 537.402,
      "text": "One was a public policy against a whole category\nof agreement."
    },
    {
      "start": 537.452,
      "end": 542.578,
      "text": "The other was the ordinary law of contracts,\napplied to specific pieces of paper."
    },
    {
      "start": 542.628,
      "end": 545.572,
      "text": "Brown One also said something about admission day."
    },
    {
      "start": 545.622,
      "end": 549.926,
      "text": "The process of signing paperwork for medical care\n— specifically,"
    },
    {
      "start": 549.676,
      "end": 554.444,
      "text": "a contract for admission to a nursing home —\nis often fraught with urgency,"
    },
    {
      "start": 554.194,
      "end": 555.903,
      "text": "confusion, and stress."
    },
    {
      "start": 555.953,
      "end": 557.699,
      "text": "Most patients, it wrote,"
    },
    {
      "start": 557.449,
      "end": 562.063,
      "text": "do not view the admission process as an interstate\ncommercial transaction"
    },
    {
      "start": 561.813,
      "end": 564.284,
      "text": "with far-reaching legal consequences."
    },
    {
      "start": 564.334,
      "end": 568.838,
      "text": "A year later, in the opinion it wrote\nafter Washington sent the cases back,"
    },
    {
      "start": 568.588,
      "end": 570.389,
      "text": "it added two more sentences."
    },
    {
      "start": 570.439,
      "end": 574.808,
      "text": "Nursing homes daily sign contracts with patients\nas a routine course"
    },
    {
      "start": 574.558,
      "end": 575.844,
      "text": "of doing business."
    },
    {
      "start": 575.894,
      "end": 580.41,
      "text": "People seek medical care in a nursing home\nfor long-term treatment to heal,"
    },
    {
      "start": 580.16,
      "end": 582.321,
      "text": "and do so only a few times in life."
    },
    {
      "start": 582.371,
      "end": 586.615,
      "text": "The doctrine underneath all that is old,\nand narrower than it sounds."
    },
    {
      "start": 586.665,
      "end": 589.421,
      "text": "Because of an overall and gross imbalance,"
    },
    {
      "start": 589.171,
      "end": 592.219,
      "text": "one-sidedness or lop-sidedness in a contract,"
    },
    {
      "start": 591.969,
      "end": 596.482,
      "text": "a court may be justified in refusing to enforce\nthe contract as written."
    },
    {
      "start": 596.532,
      "end": 599.986,
      "text": "That is unconscionability — a rule\nabout contracts."
    },
    {
      "start": 600.036,
      "end": 604.093,
      "text": "In Brown's paper and Taylor's, whoever filed paid\nto file,"
    },
    {
      "start": 603.843,
      "end": 608.852,
      "text": "and the opinion names no sum. The court\nwas careful about what it was not saying."
    },
    {
      "start": 608.902,
      "end": 611.371,
      "text": "The courts of this State, it wrote,"
    },
    {
      "start": 611.121,
      "end": 614.911,
      "text": "are not hostile to arbitration or to adhesion\ncontracts."
    },
    {
      "start": 614.961,
      "end": 619.259,
      "text": "We are hostile toward contracts of adhesion\nthat are unconscionable"
    },
    {
      "start": 619.009,
      "end": 623.136,
      "text": "and rely upon arbitration as an artifice\nto defraud a weaker party"
    },
    {
      "start": 622.886,
      "end": 628.235,
      "text": "of rights clearly provided by the common law\nor statute. The word is adhesion."
    },
    {
      "start": 628.285,
      "end": 633.625,
      "text": "A contract of adhesion is one drafted and imposed\nby a party of superior strength"
    },
    {
      "start": 633.375,
      "end": 637.298,
      "text": "that leaves the subscribing party little\nor no opportunity"
    },
    {
      "start": 637.048,
      "end": 639.295,
      "text": "to alter the substantive terms,"
    },
    {
      "start": 639.045,
      "end": 643.303,
      "text": "and only the opportunity to adhere to the contract\nor reject it."
    },
    {
      "start": 643.353,
      "end": 648.315,
      "text": "Two of these three forms said the same thing.\nThe third made no exceptions at all."
    },
    {
      "start": 648.365,
      "end": 649.962,
      "text": "Take it or leave it."
    },
    {
      "start": 650.012,
      "end": 652.412,
      "text": "The state court's finding, in Brown One:"
    },
    {
      "start": 652.162,
      "end": 655.187,
      "text": "people being admitted to long-term care facilities"
    },
    {
      "start": 654.937,
      "end": 659.629,
      "text": "and their families have to sign admission\ncontracts without time to comparison shop"
    },
    {
      "start": 659.379,
      "end": 662.569,
      "text": "or to negotiate the best service and price\ncombination."
    },
    {
      "start": 662.619,
      "end": 665.655,
      "text": "Is a take-it-or-leave-it form enough on its own?"
    },
    {
      "start": 665.705,
      "end": 668.881,
      "text": "Being a form is not a verdict, and the court said\nso."
    },
    {
      "start": 668.931,
      "end": 673.669,
      "text": "Finding that there is an adhesion contract\nis the beginning point for analysis,"
    },
    {
      "start": 673.419,
      "end": 674.661,
      "text": "not the end of it."
    },
    {
      "start": 674.711,
      "end": 678.56,
      "text": "What courts aim at doing is distinguishing good\nadhesion contracts"
    },
    {
      "start": 678.31,
      "end": 682.345,
      "text": "which should be enforced, from bad adhesion\ncontracts which should not."
    },
    {
      "start": 682.395,
      "end": 685.989,
      "text": "And then the sentence that gives the whole opinion\nits edge."
    },
    {
      "start": 686.039,
      "end": 690.464,
      "text": "It may be disingenuous for a nursing home to later\nassert that the patient"
    },
    {
      "start": 690.214,
      "end": 692.161,
      "text": "or family member consciously,"
    },
    {
      "start": 691.911,
      "end": 696.329,
      "text": "knowingly and deliberately accepted an arbitration\nclause in the contract,"
    },
    {
      "start": 696.079,
      "end": 700.683,
      "text": "and understood the clause was intended\nto eliminate their access to the courts"
    },
    {
      "start": 700.433,
      "end": 705.675,
      "text": "if the nursing home negligently injured or killed\nthe patient. Disingenuous."
    },
    {
      "start": 705.725,
      "end": 710.015,
      "text": "The defendant nursing homes in all three cases\nsought review in Washington."
    },
    {
      "start": 710.065,
      "end": 714.913,
      "text": "Two petitions for certiorari, docketed\nas 11-391 and 11-394."
    },
    {
      "start": 714.963,
      "end": 718.65,
      "text": "And the defendants specifically challenged\nSyllabus Point 21."
    },
    {
      "start": 718.7,
      "end": 721.086,
      "text": "Not the unconscionability holding."
    },
    {
      "start": 721.136,
      "end": 725.819,
      "text": "Not the ruling on the statute, which had gone\ntheir way. The timing rule."
    },
    {
      "start": 727.369,
      "end": 730.452,
      "text": "West Virginia had described Washington first."
    },
    {
      "start": 730.502,
      "end": 734.885,
      "text": "The state court had to decide whether its public\npolicy was preempted,"
    },
    {
      "start": 734.635,
      "end": 738.322,
      "text": "and to do that it read the Supreme Court's\narbitration cases."
    },
    {
      "start": 738.372,
      "end": 740.084,
      "text": "It found them unpersuasive,"
    },
    {
      "start": 739.834,
      "end": 743.452,
      "text": "in language appellate judges do not use\nabout the court above them."
    },
    {
      "start": 743.502,
      "end": 747.839,
      "text": "It called this Court's interpretation\nof the Federal Arbitration Act tendentious."
    },
    {
      "start": 747.889,
      "end": 750.554,
      "text": "It called it created from whole cloth."
    },
    {
      "start": 750.604,
      "end": 754.105,
      "text": "The sentence behind the first of those words\nis in Brown One."
    },
    {
      "start": 754.155,
      "end": 756.072,
      "text": "With tendentious reasoning,"
    },
    {
      "start": 755.822,
      "end": 760.166,
      "text": "the United States Supreme Court has stretched\nthe application of the FAA"
    },
    {
      "start": 759.916,
      "end": 764.76,
      "text": "from being a procedural statutory scheme effective\nonly in the federal courts,"
    },
    {
      "start": 764.51,
      "end": 768.789,
      "text": "to being a substantive law that preempts state law\nin both the federal"
    },
    {
      "start": 768.539,
      "end": 769.777,
      "text": "and state courts."
    },
    {
      "start": 769.827,
      "end": 774.349,
      "text": "Underneath the insult was a theory of the statute,\nand the state court laid it out."
    },
    {
      "start": 774.399,
      "end": 777.138,
      "text": "The text of the Federal Arbitration Act,"
    },
    {
      "start": 776.888,
      "end": 781.206,
      "text": "and the congressional history at the time\nof its adoption in 1925,"
    },
    {
      "start": 780.956,
      "end": 785.592,
      "text": "suggested to it that the Act was intended\nto reverse judicial hostility"
    },
    {
      "start": 785.342,
      "end": 788.564,
      "text": "to arbitration. It was designed, the court said,"
    },
    {
      "start": 788.314,
      "end": 792.316,
      "text": "to allow commercial entities engaged in interstate\ncommerce to enter"
    },
    {
      "start": 792.066,
      "end": 797.354,
      "text": "into arbitration agreements that would be enforced\nnationwide. Commercial entities."
    },
    {
      "start": 797.404,
      "end": 799.001,
      "text": "Nationwide enforcement."
    },
    {
      "start": 799.051,
      "end": 802.738,
      "text": "Then it read the recent decisions and said what it\nthought they were doing."
    },
    {
      "start": 802.788,
      "end": 805.363,
      "text": "Much of the reasoning was tendentious,"
    },
    {
      "start": 805.113,
      "end": 808.403,
      "text": "and intended to promote a particular point of view\n—"
    },
    {
      "start": 808.153,
      "end": 812.466,
      "text": "namely that arbitration is a panacea for all\nthe woes of litigation"
    },
    {
      "start": 812.216,
      "end": 816.527,
      "text": "and should therefore be given special favor.\nA panacea."
    },
    {
      "start": 816.577,
      "end": 821.298,
      "text": "And from that reading, the state court drew\nthe finding it would be reversed for:"
    },
    {
      "start": 821.048,
      "end": 823.975,
      "text": "that the Supreme Court had never extended the Act"
    },
    {
      "start": 823.725,
      "end": 827.369,
      "text": "to arbitration agreements like the ones\nin these three cases."
    },
    {
      "start": 827.419,
      "end": 829.387,
      "text": "Then the conclusion it reached."
    },
    {
      "start": 829.437,
      "end": 832.668,
      "text": "Congress did not intend for the FAA to be, in any\nway,"
    },
    {
      "start": 832.418,
      "end": 837.532,
      "text": "applicable to personal injury or wrongful death\nsuits that only collaterally derive"
    },
    {
      "start": 837.282,
      "end": 842.272,
      "text": "from a written agreement that evidences\na transaction affecting interstate commerce."
    },
    {
      "start": 842.322,
      "end": 847.238,
      "text": "Collaterally derive. Is a negligence claim really\na claim on the contract?"
    },
    {
      "start": 847.288,
      "end": 851.021,
      "text": "It arrives later, out of an event nobody\ncontracted about."
    },
    {
      "start": 851.071,
      "end": 856.337,
      "text": "The Supreme Court granted certiorari and decided\nboth cases on February 21, 2012."
    },
    {
      "start": 856.387,
      "end": 861.302,
      "text": "Five pages, per curiam. It opened with the rule\nand left the courtesies out."
    },
    {
      "start": 861.352,
      "end": 866.057,
      "text": "State and federal courts must enforce the Federal\nArbitration Act with respect"
    },
    {
      "start": 865.807,
      "end": 869.079,
      "text": "to all arbitration agreements covered\nby that statute."
    },
    {
      "start": 869.129,
      "end": 872.463,
      "text": "Here, the Supreme Court of Appeals of West\nVirginia,"
    },
    {
      "start": 872.213,
      "end": 877.364,
      "text": "by misreading and disregarding the precedents\nof this Court interpreting the FAA,"
    },
    {
      "start": 877.114,
      "end": 881.732,
      "text": "did not follow controlling federal law\nimplementing that basic principle."
    },
    {
      "start": 881.782,
      "end": 887.069,
      "text": "Misreading and disregarding. Two words, and they\nare not the same accusation."
    },
    {
      "start": 887.119,
      "end": 890.177,
      "text": "One is error. The other is choice."
    },
    {
      "start": 890.227,
      "end": 894.889,
      "text": "The Court then described what the state court\nhad done, in a single sentence."
    },
    {
      "start": 894.939,
      "end": 899.897,
      "text": "The state court held unenforceable all predispute\narbitration agreements that apply"
    },
    {
      "start": 899.647,
      "end": 904.152,
      "text": "to claims alleging personal injury or wrongful\ndeath against nursing homes."
    },
    {
      "start": 904.202,
      "end": 908.142,
      "text": "All of them. Next, the statute."
    },
    {
      "start": 908.192,
      "end": 912.811,
      "text": "Section 2 of the Federal Arbitration Act, quoted\nin the opinion:"
    },
    {
      "start": 912.561,
      "end": 918.177,
      "text": "a written provision in a contract evidencing\na transaction involving commerce"
    },
    {
      "start": 917.927,
      "end": 923.486,
      "text": "to settle by arbitration a controversy thereafter\narising out of such contract"
    },
    {
      "start": 923.236,
      "end": 927.74,
      "text": "or transaction shall be valid, irrevocable,\nand enforceable,"
    },
    {
      "start": 927.49,
      "end": 932.356,
      "text": "save upon such grounds as exist at law\nor in equity for the revocation"
    },
    {
      "start": 932.106,
      "end": 936.002,
      "text": "of any contract. Valid, irrevocable,\nand enforceable."
    },
    {
      "start": 936.052,
      "end": 939.208,
      "text": "And then, in the same sentence of the statute,"
    },
    {
      "start": 938.958,
      "end": 944.171,
      "text": "the exception that decides everything\nthat follows. Keep the second half."
    },
    {
      "start": 944.221,
      "end": 948.114,
      "text": "It comes back. On the first half the Court\nwas brief."
    },
    {
      "start": 948.164,
      "end": 951.556,
      "text": "The statute's text includes no exception\nfor personal-injury"
    },
    {
      "start": 951.306,
      "end": 952.872,
      "text": "or wrongful-death claims."
    },
    {
      "start": 952.922,
      "end": 958.13,
      "text": "The Act requires courts to enforce the bargain\nof the parties to arbitrate —"
    },
    {
      "start": 957.88,
      "end": 962.135,
      "text": "a line from a 1985 decision, Dean Witter Reynolds\nagainst Byrd."
    },
    {
      "start": 962.185,
      "end": 967.682,
      "text": "It reflects an emphatic federal policy in favor\nof arbitral dispute resolution —"
    },
    {
      "start": 967.432,
      "end": 972.18,
      "text": "a line the Court took from one of its own per\ncuriam opinions of 2011,"
    },
    {
      "start": 971.93,
      "end": 975.16,
      "text": "which was itself quoting a decision from 1985."
    },
    {
      "start": 975.21,
      "end": 978.2,
      "text": "Then the precedent that made the answer\nmechanical."
    },
    {
      "start": 978.25,
      "end": 983.3,
      "text": "When state law prohibits outright the arbitration\nof a particular type of claim,"
    },
    {
      "start": 983.05,
      "end": 987.927,
      "text": "the analysis is straightforward: the conflicting\nrule is displaced by the FAA."
    },
    {
      "start": 987.977,
      "end": 992.546,
      "text": "That was AT&T Mobility against Concepcion, decided\nthe previous term."
    },
    {
      "start": 992.596,
      "end": 994.796,
      "text": "That rule resolves these cases."
    },
    {
      "start": 994.846,
      "end": 999.415,
      "text": "Four words, and then the application,\nin the Court's own sentence."
    },
    {
      "start": 999.465,
      "end": 1003.151,
      "text": "West Virginia's prohibition against predispute\nagreements"
    },
    {
      "start": 1002.901,
      "end": 1004.891,
      "text": "to arbitrate personal-injury"
    },
    {
      "start": 1004.641,
      "end": 1009.649,
      "text": "or wrongful-death claims against nursing homes\nis a categorical rule prohibiting"
    },
    {
      "start": 1009.399,
      "end": 1012.187,
      "text": "arbitration of a particular type of claim,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1011.937,
      "end": 1015.83,
      "text": "and that rule is contrary to the terms\nand coverage of the FAA."
    },
    {
      "start": 1015.88,
      "end": 1020.981,
      "text": "Had a state tried this before? The Court listed\nfour that had, and lost."
    },
    {
      "start": 1021.031,
      "end": 1023.107,
      "text": "Preston against Ferrer, 2008 —"
    },
    {
      "start": 1022.857,
      "end": 1027.733,
      "text": "a state commissioner given exclusive jurisdiction\nover an issue the parties"
    },
    {
      "start": 1027.483,
      "end": 1029.269,
      "text": "had agreed to arbitrate."
    },
    {
      "start": 1029.319,
      "end": 1031.079,
      "text": "Mastrobuono, 1995 —"
    },
    {
      "start": 1030.829,
      "end": 1037.185,
      "text": "a state rule requiring judicial resolution\nof claims involving punitive damages."
    },
    {
      "start": 1037.235,
      "end": 1039.237,
      "text": "Perry against Thomas, 1987 —"
    },
    {
      "start": 1038.987,
      "end": 1044.265,
      "text": "a state requirement that litigants be provided\na judicial forum for wage disputes."
    },
    {
      "start": 1044.315,
      "end": 1046.712,
      "text": "Southland against Keating, 1984 —"
    },
    {
      "start": 1046.462,
      "end": 1051.438,
      "text": "a state investment statute banning arbitration\nof claims brought under it."
    },
    {
      "start": 1051.488,
      "end": 1056.585,
      "text": "Preempted. Preempted. Preempted. Preempted."
    },
    {
      "start": 1056.635,
      "end": 1060.275,
      "text": "To the language about tendentious reasoning, one\nsentence."
    },
    {
      "start": 1060.325,
      "end": 1064.678,
      "text": "The West Virginia court's interpretation\nof the FAA was both incorrect"
    },
    {
      "start": 1064.428,
      "end": 1068.841,
      "text": "and inconsistent with clear instruction\nin the precedents of this Court."
    },
    {
      "start": 1068.891,
      "end": 1070.873,
      "text": "Then the constitutional point,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1070.623,
      "end": 1074.064,
      "text": "which is the shortest passage in the opinion\nand the largest."
    },
    {
      "start": 1074.114,
      "end": 1077.835,
      "text": "When this Court has fulfilled its duty\nto interpret federal law,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1077.585,
      "end": 1081.934,
      "text": "a state court may not contradict or fail\nto implement the rule so established."
    },
    {
      "start": 1081.984,
      "end": 1084.324,
      "text": "The citation is the Supremacy Clause."
    },
    {
      "start": 1084.374,
      "end": 1088.246,
      "text": "The decision of the State Supreme Court of Appeals\nmust be vacated."
    },
    {
      "start": 1089.796,
      "end": 1093.575,
      "text": "To vacate a judgment is to wipe it out and send\nthe case back."
    },
    {
      "start": 1093.625,
      "end": 1096.29,
      "text": "It is not a ruling that the other side wins."
    },
    {
      "start": 1096.34,
      "end": 1100.849,
      "text": "And here the Supreme Court was unusually explicit\nabout how much it was leaving"
    },
    {
      "start": 1100.599,
      "end": 1104.924,
      "text": "undone, because it wrote a second part. Part Two\nis one page long."
    },
    {
      "start": 1104.974,
      "end": 1108.15,
      "text": "It begins with the holding nobody had appealed."
    },
    {
      "start": 1108.2,
      "end": 1111.557,
      "text": "The West Virginia court proposed an alternative\nholding"
    },
    {
      "start": 1111.307,
      "end": 1114.638,
      "text": "that the particular arbitration clauses in Brown's\ncase"
    },
    {
      "start": 1114.388,
      "end": 1116.809,
      "text": "and Taylor's case were unconscionable."
    },
    {
      "start": 1116.859,
      "end": 1121.271,
      "text": "As to Marchio, the Supreme Court added a note\ninside its own sentence:"
    },
    {
      "start": 1121.021,
      "end": 1126.007,
      "text": "the state court had not addressed the question\nwhether the arbitration agreement"
    },
    {
      "start": 1125.757,
      "end": 1130.251,
      "text": "in Marchio's case is unenforceable for reasons\nother than public policy."
    },
    {
      "start": 1130.301,
      "end": 1135.657,
      "text": "Two of the three papers had been condemned twice —\nonce by a categorical rule,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1135.407,
      "end": 1137.61,
      "text": "once by ordinary contract law."
    },
    {
      "start": 1137.66,
      "end": 1142.095,
      "text": "The third had been condemned once,\non the categorical rule alone,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1141.845,
      "end": 1144.504,
      "text": "and examined on no other ground at all."
    },
    {
      "start": 1144.554,
      "end": 1148.148,
      "text": "The Court's problem with the alternative holding\nwas contamination."
    },
    {
      "start": 1148.198,
      "end": 1149.827,
      "text": "It is unclear, however,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1149.577,
      "end": 1154.685,
      "text": "to what degree the state court's alternative\nholding was influenced by the invalid,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1154.435,
      "end": 1156.705,
      "text": "categorical rule discussed above,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1156.455,
      "end": 1161.565,
      "text": "the rule against predispute arbitration\nagreements. And it produced the example."
    },
    {
      "start": 1161.615,
      "end": 1164.867,
      "text": "In its discussion of the alternative holding,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1164.617,
      "end": 1169.464,
      "text": "the state court had found the arbitration clauses\nunconscionable in part"
    },
    {
      "start": 1169.214,
      "end": 1172.231,
      "text": "because a predispute arbitration agreement"
    },
    {
      "start": 1171.981,
      "end": 1175.054,
      "text": "of this kind clearly violates public policy."
    },
    {
      "start": 1175.104,
      "end": 1179.078,
      "text": "There it was, sitting in the middle\nof the contract analysis:"
    },
    {
      "start": 1178.828,
      "end": 1181.392,
      "text": "the rule that had just been struck out,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1181.142,
      "end": 1185.431,
      "text": "doing work inside the finding that was supposed\nto stand without it."
    },
    {
      "start": 1185.481,
      "end": 1187.217,
      "text": "So, the instruction."
    },
    {
      "start": 1187.267,
      "end": 1191.121,
      "text": "On remand, the West Virginia court must consider\nwhether,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1190.871,
      "end": 1193.321,
      "text": "absent that general public policy,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1193.071,
      "end": 1195.791,
      "text": "the arbitration clauses in Brown's case"
    },
    {
      "start": 1195.541,
      "end": 1200.191,
      "text": "and Taylor's case are unenforceable under state\ncommon law principles"
    },
    {
      "start": 1199.941,
      "end": 1204.096,
      "text": "that are not specific to arbitration\nand pre-empted by the FAA."
    },
    {
      "start": 1204.146,
      "end": 1207.879,
      "text": "The last clause is the savings clause from section\n2, back again."
    },
    {
      "start": 1207.929,
      "end": 1210.587,
      "text": "A state may not write a rule that says:"
    },
    {
      "start": 1210.337,
      "end": 1213.334,
      "text": "this type of claim does not go to arbitration."
    },
    {
      "start": 1213.384,
      "end": 1217.256,
      "text": "That is what West Virginia had written,\nand that is what fell."
    },
    {
      "start": 1217.306,
      "end": 1220.912,
      "text": "A state may say: this contract is unconscionable,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1220.662,
      "end": 1224.495,
      "text": "and we would say so of any contract\nwith these features,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1224.245,
      "end": 1228.051,
      "text": "whether or not the word arbitration ever appeared\nin it."
    },
    {
      "start": 1228.101,
      "end": 1233.574,
      "text": "That is exactly the ground section 2 preserves,\nin terms. Then the disposition."
    },
    {
      "start": 1233.624,
      "end": 1236.15,
      "text": "The petition for certiorari is granted."
    },
    {
      "start": 1236.2,
      "end": 1240.578,
      "text": "The judgment of the Supreme Court of Appeals\nof West Virginia is vacated,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1240.328,
      "end": 1244.902,
      "text": "and the cases are remanded for proceedings\nnot inconsistent with this opinion."
    },
    {
      "start": 1244.952,
      "end": 1247.24,
      "text": "The Supreme Court did not hold that any"
    },
    {
      "start": 1246.99,
      "end": 1249.66,
      "text": "of these three arbitration clauses was valid."
    },
    {
      "start": 1249.71,
      "end": 1252.561,
      "text": "It did not order anyone to arbitrate anything."
    },
    {
      "start": 1252.611,
      "end": 1255.478,
      "text": "It did not decide whether these families\ncould sue,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1255.228,
      "end": 1259.521,
      "text": "and it did not decide whether the papers they\nwere holding meant what the nursing"
    },
    {
      "start": 1259.271,
      "end": 1260.663,
      "text": "homes said they meant."
    },
    {
      "start": 1260.713,
      "end": 1264.343,
      "text": "It held that one rule West Virginia had invented\nwas preempted,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1264.093,
      "end": 1269.436,
      "text": "and that a judgment resting on that rule\ncould not stand. Everything else went back."
    },
    {
      "start": 1269.486,
      "end": 1273.345,
      "text": "It also left untouched a question the record\ndoes not answer:"
    },
    {
      "start": 1273.095,
      "end": 1277.642,
      "text": "whether a relative's signature on an admission\nform can bind a patient,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1277.392,
      "end": 1282.25,
      "text": "or a patient's estate, at all. That question\nwas raised in the litigation."
    },
    {
      "start": 1282.3,
      "end": 1286.24,
      "text": "It is in the file. The five pages do not mention\nit."
    },
    {
      "start": 1286.29,
      "end": 1291.762,
      "text": "And the opinion says nothing whatever\nabout a contract that arbitrates a death claim"
    },
    {
      "start": 1291.512,
      "end": 1296.732,
      "text": "while leaving a debt claim in a courthouse.\nThat clause was in front of the Court."
    },
    {
      "start": 1296.782,
      "end": 1300.097,
      "text": "It is quoted in the Court's own recitation\nof the facts."
    },
    {
      "start": 1300.147,
      "end": 1305.48,
      "text": "It was not what the defendants had challenged.\nThis was a per curiam opinion."
    },
    {
      "start": 1305.53,
      "end": 1307.73,
      "text": "Per curiam means by the court."
    },
    {
      "start": 1307.78,
      "end": 1312.535,
      "text": "There is no author, no reported vote,\nand no separate writing attached to the text."
    },
    {
      "start": 1312.585,
      "end": 1314.943,
      "text": "It is not a synonym for unanimous,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1314.693,
      "end": 1318.544,
      "text": "and nobody should be told which Justices stood\nbehind it,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1318.294,
      "end": 1320.683,
      "text": "because the document does not say."
    },
    {
      "start": 1320.733,
      "end": 1323.924,
      "text": "So the file went back to Charleston with a mandate\nin it,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1323.674,
      "end": 1326.602,
      "text": "and an unanswered question underneath the mandate."
    },
    {
      "start": 1326.652,
      "end": 1329.921,
      "text": "The West Virginia court did not treat\nthat as a formality."
    },
    {
      "start": 1329.971,
      "end": 1332.113,
      "text": "In an order dated April 3, 2012,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1331.863,
      "end": 1336.165,
      "text": "it directed the parties to submit additional\nbriefs and arguments."
    },
    {
      "start": 1336.215,
      "end": 1338.09,
      "text": "It heard the cases again."
    },
    {
      "start": 1338.14,
      "end": 1339.378,
      "text": "At that rehearing,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1339.128,
      "end": 1341.17,
      "text": "counsel for the plaintiffs argued"
    },
    {
      "start": 1340.92,
      "end": 1345.361,
      "text": "that because the trial courts had never permitted\nthe parties to develop evidence"
    },
    {
      "start": 1345.111,
      "end": 1349.675,
      "text": "on unconscionability, parties challenging\nan arbitration clause must have a right"
    },
    {
      "start": 1349.425,
      "end": 1353.876,
      "text": "to conduct discovery. Counsel for Marmet Health\nCare Center argued the reverse."
    },
    {
      "start": 1353.926,
      "end": 1356.215,
      "text": "Brown One had been wrong, they said,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1355.965,
      "end": 1360.454,
      "text": "because there was insufficient evidence\nin the record to support a finding"
    },
    {
      "start": 1360.204,
      "end": 1363.232,
      "text": "that the arbitration clause was unconscionable."
    },
    {
      "start": 1363.282,
      "end": 1367.108,
      "text": "Both sides, in other words, were now arguing\nabout an empty file."
    },
    {
      "start": 1367.158,
      "end": 1372.816,
      "text": "The cases were submitted on June 6, 2012.\nThe opinion came down seven days later."
    },
    {
      "start": 1374.366,
      "end": 1376.288,
      "text": "June 13, 2012."
    },
    {
      "start": 1376.338,
      "end": 1381.532,
      "text": "Ketchum, Chief Justice, writing for the West\nVirginia court, in the second opinion —"
    },
    {
      "start": 1381.282,
      "end": 1386.826,
      "text": "the one that followed Brown One. The first move\nis obedience, and it is exact."
    },
    {
      "start": 1386.876,
      "end": 1390.013,
      "text": "In accordance with the Supreme Court's mandate,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1389.763,
      "end": 1393.788,
      "text": "we overrule Syllabus Point 21 of Brown One.\nOverrule."
    },
    {
      "start": 1393.838,
      "end": 1396.456,
      "text": "Not vacate, not modify, not distinguish."
    },
    {
      "start": 1396.506,
      "end": 1400.265,
      "text": "The holding that had gone to Washington was taken\nout of West Virginia law"
    },
    {
      "start": 1400.015,
      "end": 1404.301,
      "text": "by the court that had written it. So had West\nVirginia simply surrendered?"
    },
    {
      "start": 1404.351,
      "end": 1406.784,
      "text": "The next sentence, in the same paragraph:"
    },
    {
      "start": 1406.834,
      "end": 1410.819,
      "text": "We otherwise find that the Supreme Court's\ndecision does not counsel us"
    },
    {
      "start": 1410.569,
      "end": 1414.607,
      "text": "to alter our original analysis of West Virginia's\ncommon law of contracts."
    },
    {
      "start": 1414.657,
      "end": 1416.026,
      "text": "And then, plainly:"
    },
    {
      "start": 1415.776,
      "end": 1420.108,
      "text": "we otherwise reaffirm all of our discussion\nand holdings in Brown One."
    },
    {
      "start": 1420.158,
      "end": 1422.415,
      "text": "And in the next paragraph: however,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1422.165,
      "end": 1425.678,
      "text": "in light of the parties' additional briefs\nand arguments,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1425.428,
      "end": 1430.506,
      "text": "we modify our conclusions in Brown One. Both\nsentences are in the same opinion."
    },
    {
      "start": 1430.556,
      "end": 1433.917,
      "text": "The state court had noticed something\nabout the five pages."
    },
    {
      "start": 1433.967,
      "end": 1438.935,
      "text": "The Supreme Court's opinion did not discuss any\nother portion of Brown One,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1438.685,
      "end": 1442.39,
      "text": "aside from Syllabus Point 21 and its accompanying\ntext."
    },
    {
      "start": 1442.44,
      "end": 1444.966,
      "text": "One holding out of three had been reversed."
    },
    {
      "start": 1445.016,
      "end": 1446.778,
      "text": "The other two were untouched,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1446.528,
      "end": 1450.003,
      "text": "and the court that wrote them declined to read\nsilence as defeat."
    },
    {
      "start": 1450.053,
      "end": 1451.54,
      "text": "On the first of them:"
    },
    {
      "start": 1451.29,
      "end": 1455.47,
      "text": "the parties have not challenged our holding\nin Syllabus Point 11"
    },
    {
      "start": 1455.22,
      "end": 1460.28,
      "text": "of Brown One regarding the preemption of section\n15(c) by section 2 of the FAA,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1460.03,
      "end": 1461.913,
      "text": "and we need not revisit it."
    },
    {
      "start": 1461.963,
      "end": 1465.193,
      "text": "It then described the doctrine it was keeping,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1464.943,
      "end": 1468.064,
      "text": "in the exact vocabulary the mandate had used."
    },
    {
      "start": 1468.114,
      "end": 1473.809,
      "text": "The doctrine of unconscionability that we\nexplicated in Brown One is a general,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1473.559,
      "end": 1479.225,
      "text": "state, common-law, contract-law principle\nthat is not specific to arbitration,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1478.975,
      "end": 1481.321,
      "text": "and does not implicate the FAA."
    },
    {
      "start": 1481.371,
      "end": 1485.336,
      "text": "And the court did not take back the language\nthat had got it reversed."
    },
    {
      "start": 1485.386,
      "end": 1488.422,
      "text": "Here is how it described what had happened to it."
    },
    {
      "start": 1488.472,
      "end": 1489.933,
      "text": "The Supreme Court —"
    },
    {
      "start": 1489.683,
      "end": 1494.383,
      "text": "without elucidating how and why the FAA applies\nto negligence actions"
    },
    {
      "start": 1494.133,
      "end": 1497.323,
      "text": "that arise subsequently and only incidentally"
    },
    {
      "start": 1497.073,
      "end": 1500.34,
      "text": "to a contract containing an arbitration clause —"
    },
    {
      "start": 1500.09,
      "end": 1505.481,
      "text": "summarily concluded that the holding\nwas a categorical rule contrary to the terms"
    },
    {
      "start": 1505.231,
      "end": 1510.824,
      "text": "and coverage of the FAA. Summarily. Without\nelucidating how and why."
    },
    {
      "start": 1510.874,
      "end": 1515.388,
      "text": "That is a court accepting a result while declining\nto accept the reasoning,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1515.138,
      "end": 1517.858,
      "text": "in the very document it was ordered to write."
    },
    {
      "start": 1517.908,
      "end": 1522.485,
      "text": "What it kept was the body of contract law it\nhad assembled in 2011 —"
    },
    {
      "start": 1522.235,
      "end": 1526.517,
      "text": "the adhesion analysis, the sliding scale,\nthe whole apparatus."
    },
    {
      "start": 1526.567,
      "end": 1529.878,
      "text": "On the sliding scale, in the words it reaffirmed:"
    },
    {
      "start": 1529.628,
      "end": 1533.59,
      "text": "a contract term is unenforceable if it is both\nprocedurally"
    },
    {
      "start": 1533.34,
      "end": 1538.752,
      "text": "and substantively unconscionable, but both need\nnot be present to the same degree."
    },
    {
      "start": 1538.802,
      "end": 1542.229,
      "text": "The more substantively oppressive the contract\nterm,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1541.979,
      "end": 1546.421,
      "text": "the less evidence of procedural unconscionability\nis required to come"
    },
    {
      "start": 1546.171,
      "end": 1550.337,
      "text": "to the conclusion that the clause\nis unenforceable, and vice versa."
    },
    {
      "start": 1550.387,
      "end": 1553.981,
      "text": "On the substance of a term, this is the sentence\nit kept."
    },
    {
      "start": 1554.031,
      "end": 1557.847,
      "text": "Substantive unconscionability may manifest itself\nin the form"
    },
    {
      "start": 1557.597,
      "end": 1562.269,
      "text": "of an agreement requiring arbitration only\nfor the claims of the weaker party."
    },
    {
      "start": 1562.319,
      "end": 1565.82,
      "text": "But a choice of forums for the claims\nof the stronger party."
    },
    {
      "start": 1565.87,
      "end": 1568.533,
      "text": "Agreements to arbitrate, the court wrote,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1568.283,
      "end": 1572.668,
      "text": "must contain at least a modicum of bilaterality\nto avoid unconscionability."
    },
    {
      "start": 1573.018,
      "end": 1577.355,
      "text": "The West Virginia court did not apply\nthat doctrine to that clause in this opinion."
    },
    {
      "start": 1577.405,
      "end": 1580.023,
      "text": "It could not, and it said why."
    },
    {
      "start": 1580.073,
      "end": 1583.434,
      "text": "It had a sentence of the Supreme Court's own\nto lean on."
    },
    {
      "start": 1583.484,
      "end": 1585.34,
      "text": "Claims of coercion, fraud,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1585.09,
      "end": 1589.924,
      "text": "or unequal bargaining power in the formation\nof an arbitration agreement are,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1589.674,
      "end": 1593.579,
      "text": "that Court has said, best left for resolution\nin specific cases."
    },
    {
      "start": 1593.629,
      "end": 1596.352,
      "text": "Given that position, the state court wrote,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1596.102,
      "end": 1600.195,
      "text": "further development of the factual record\nby the parties is proper."
    },
    {
      "start": 1600.245,
      "end": 1603.281,
      "text": "Then its own account of the two records in front\nof it."
    },
    {
      "start": 1603.331,
      "end": 1608.112,
      "text": "The circuit court's order in Brown's case\nis devoid of any findings of fact"
    },
    {
      "start": 1607.862,
      "end": 1611.615,
      "text": "or conclusions of law on the question\nof unconscionability."
    },
    {
      "start": 1611.665,
      "end": 1614.214,
      "text": "Taylor's order had some findings of fact,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1613.964,
      "end": 1618.971,
      "text": "but that court had never comprehensively analysed\nthe question under the guidelines"
    },
    {
      "start": 1618.721,
      "end": 1620.831,
      "text": "the state court laid down in 2011."
    },
    {
      "start": 1620.881,
      "end": 1625.45,
      "text": "There was no evidence to weigh, because nobody\nhad been permitted to take any."
    },
    {
      "start": 1625.5,
      "end": 1629.157,
      "text": "Its own line for a record in that condition,\nfrom Brown One:"
    },
    {
      "start": 1628.907,
      "end": 1631.23,
      "text": "without factual or legal findings,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1630.98,
      "end": 1634.388,
      "text": "this Court is greatly at sea without a chart\nor compass."
    },
    {
      "start": 1634.438,
      "end": 1639.725,
      "text": "So it sent both cases down rather than answering\nthem. In its own words."
    },
    {
      "start": 1639.775,
      "end": 1644.162,
      "text": "We conclude the correct course is to remand\nthese cases to the circuit courts"
    },
    {
      "start": 1643.912,
      "end": 1647.362,
      "text": "for the taking of evidence, the full development\nof a record,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1647.112,
      "end": 1650.985,
      "text": "and proper consideration of whether the clauses\nare unconscionable."
    },
    {
      "start": 1651.035,
      "end": 1655.341,
      "text": "Two further arguments were on the table,\nand the court refused both —"
    },
    {
      "start": 1655.091,
      "end": 1658.205,
      "text": "not on their merits, but on the order of business."
    },
    {
      "start": 1658.255,
      "end": 1662.592,
      "text": "The plaintiffs had argued that the clauses\nwere impossible to comply with."
    },
    {
      "start": 1662.642,
      "end": 1665.827,
      "text": "The Marmet clause required binding arbitration\nin accordance"
    },
    {
      "start": 1665.577,
      "end": 1669.579,
      "text": "with the Commercial Arbitration Rules\nof the American Arbitration Association."
    },
    {
      "start": 1669.629,
      "end": 1671.551,
      "text": "Effective January 1, 2003,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1671.301,
      "end": 1676.23,
      "text": "that association had announced it would no longer\naccept the administration"
    },
    {
      "start": 1675.98,
      "end": 1680.626,
      "text": "of cases involving individual patients without\na post-dispute agreement"
    },
    {
      "start": 1680.376,
      "end": 1685.176,
      "text": "to arbitrate. The Clarksburg clause required\narbitration in accordance with the Code"
    },
    {
      "start": 1684.926,
      "end": 1687.455,
      "text": "of Procedure of the National Arbitration Forum."
    },
    {
      "start": 1687.505,
      "end": 1693.356,
      "text": "That forum had announced it would cease\nto administer consumer arbitration disputes"
    },
    {
      "start": 1693.106,
      "end": 1695.232,
      "text": "as of Friday, July 24, 2009,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1694.982,
      "end": 1699.969,
      "text": "as part of a settlement agreement\nwith the Minnesota Attorney General."
    },
    {
      "start": 1700.019,
      "end": 1703.198,
      "text": "The forums named in the papers had stopped taking\nthe kind"
    },
    {
      "start": 1702.948,
      "end": 1705.006,
      "text": "of case the papers were sending them."
    },
    {
      "start": 1705.056,
      "end": 1708.789,
      "text": "The second argument is the one the Supreme Court\nnever reached."
    },
    {
      "start": 1708.839,
      "end": 1712.264,
      "text": "There is no evidence in the record, the plaintiffs\nsaid,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1712.014,
      "end": 1716.888,
      "text": "that the family member who signed each admission\nagreement had the legal authority"
    },
    {
      "start": 1716.638,
      "end": 1718.591,
      "text": "to sign an arbitration clause,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1718.341,
      "end": 1723.064,
      "text": "and thereby waive the resident's or the resident's\nheirs' right to pursue action"
    },
    {
      "start": 1722.814,
      "end": 1727.268,
      "text": "in court. We decline to consider these two\narguments, the court wrote,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1727.018,
      "end": 1730.147,
      "text": "which should be considered by the trial court\nfirst."
    },
    {
      "start": 1730.197,
      "end": 1735.531,
      "text": "Then the disposition, and it is not one thing.\nBrown: reversed and remanded."
    },
    {
      "start": 1735.581,
      "end": 1739.985,
      "text": "Taylor: the same. Marchio: the certified question\nanswered."
    },
    {
      "start": 1740.035,
      "end": 1745.115,
      "text": "Yes — the Nursing Home Act's waiver ban\nis preempted by the Federal Arbitration Act."
    },
    {
      "start": 1745.165,
      "end": 1748.819,
      "text": "Unconscionability was left to be raised\nby the parties on remand,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1748.569,
      "end": 1751.313,
      "text": "because the trial court had never considered it."
    },
    {
      "start": 1751.363,
      "end": 1755.746,
      "text": "Nothing in that second opinion holds these clauses\nunenforceable."
    },
    {
      "start": 1755.796,
      "end": 1758.229,
      "text": "Nothing in it holds them enforceable either."
    },
    {
      "start": 1758.279,
      "end": 1763.355,
      "text": "It hands the question back to the circuit courts\nand stops. So what was the paper?"
    },
    {
      "start": 1763.405,
      "end": 1766.674,
      "text": "On the record these two opinions make, it\nwas this."
    },
    {
      "start": 1766.724,
      "end": 1770.354,
      "text": "A form signed at an admission desk by a family\nmember,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1770.104,
      "end": 1773.94,
      "text": "on behalf of a patient who required extensive\nnursing care."
    },
    {
      "start": 1773.99,
      "end": 1778.912,
      "text": "A form that sent every dispute to a private\narbitrator, except one:"
    },
    {
      "start": 1778.662,
      "end": 1784.339,
      "text": "the home's own claim for money. A form that made\nwhoever filed first pay to file."
    },
    {
      "start": 1784.389,
      "end": 1788.772,
      "text": "And in one of the three cases, a form\nwith no exceptions in it at all."
    },
    {
      "start": 1788.822,
      "end": 1791.232,
      "text": "It was, the Supreme Court held,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1790.982,
      "end": 1796.824,
      "text": "a written provision in a contract evidencing\na transaction involving commerce —"
    },
    {
      "start": 1796.574,
      "end": 1800.496,
      "text": "and therefore inside an Act of Congress passed\nin 1925."
    },
    {
      "start": 1800.546,
      "end": 1806.204,
      "text": "That is what Washington decided. It decided\nthe paper was covered by the statute."
    },
    {
      "start": 1806.254,
      "end": 1811.681,
      "text": "It did not decide the paper was good. Section 2\ncarries both halves in one sentence."
    },
    {
      "start": 1811.731,
      "end": 1816.532,
      "text": "Enforceable — and revocable on any ground\nthat would revoke any other contract."
    },
    {
      "start": 1816.582,
      "end": 1819.34,
      "text": "The savings clause was there the whole time."
    },
    {
      "start": 1819.39,
      "end": 1823.866,
      "text": "What the Supreme Court decided was that West\nVirginia had reached past it."
    },
    {
      "start": 1823.916,
      "end": 1828.677,
      "text": "West Virginia gave up the rule it\nhad been reversed on and kept everything else,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1828.427,
      "end": 1832.534,
      "text": "including the doctrine that asks\nwhether a contract is so one-sided"
    },
    {
      "start": 1832.284,
      "end": 1835.219,
      "text": "that a court may refuse to enforce it as written."
    },
    {
      "start": 1835.269,
      "end": 1840.231,
      "text": "Which leaves the story where the documents leave\nit. Three families sued."
    },
    {
      "start": 1840.281,
      "end": 1842.017,
      "text": "Three papers were signed."
    },
    {
      "start": 1842.067,
      "end": 1846.511,
      "text": "What the litigation settled was which sovereign's\nlaw applied to those papers,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1846.261,
      "end": 1849.051,
      "text": "and almost nothing about whether they were fair."
    },
    {
      "start": 1849.101,
      "end": 1852.741,
      "text": "Two questions were still standing when both\nopinions closed."
    },
    {
      "start": 1852.791,
      "end": 1857.263,
      "text": "Whether a paper that arbitrates a death\nand litigates a debt is lop-sided enough"
    },
    {
      "start": 1857.013,
      "end": 1860.007,
      "text": "that a court should refuse to enforce it\nas written."
    },
    {
      "start": 1860.057,
      "end": 1864.119,
      "text": "And whether the family member who signed it\nhad the authority to sign away anything"
    },
    {
      "start": 1863.869,
      "end": 1866.365,
      "text": "at all. Neither had been answered."
    },
    {
      "start": 1866.415,
      "end": 1870.705,
      "text": "The first was sent back down to be argued\non a record that did not exist yet."
    },
    {
      "start": 1870.755,
      "end": 1873.513,
      "text": "The second the court declined to reach at all."
    },
    {
      "start": 1873.563,
      "end": 1876.785,
      "text": "The clause, once more, as the two papers wrote it."
    },
    {
      "start": 1876.835,
      "end": 1878.501,
      "text": "To arbitrate all disputes,"
    },
    {
      "start": 1878.251,
      "end": 1881.683,
      "text": "other than claims to collect late payments owed\nby the patient."
    }
  ],
  "graphics": [],
  "figures": [
    {
      "start": 0.248,
      "end": 3.248,
      "kind": "lowerthird",
      "primary": "AI-assisted visualization",
      "secondary": "symbolic reconstruction, no real likenesses"
    },
    {
      "start": 3.544,
      "end": 6.544,
      "kind": "kinetic",
      "lines": [
        "A DISPUTE ABOUT HOW SOMEBODY DIED",
        "GOES TO A PRIVATE ARBITRATOR."
      ],
      "style": "emphasis",
      "emphasisWords": [
        "A PRIVATE ARBITRATOR"
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 6.84,
      "end": 9.84,
      "kind": "kinetic",
      "lines": [
        "A DISPUTE ABOUT AN UNPAID BILL",
        "STAYS IN A COURTHOUSE."
      ],
      "style": "emphasis",
      "emphasisWords": [
        "A COURTHOUSE"
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 11.752,
      "end": 14.752,
      "kind": "lowerthird",
      "primary": "MARMET HEALTH CARE CENTER, INC. v. BROWN",
      "secondary": "Supreme Court of the United States, decided 21 February 2012"
    },
    {
      "start": 17.88,
      "end": 20.88,
      "kind": "numberticker",
      "value": 5,
      "label": "Pages in the opinion",
      "group": false
    },
    {
      "start": 24.009,
      "end": 27.009,
      "kind": "kinetic",
      "lines": [
        "PER CURIAM.",
        "NO AUTHOR.",
        "NO VOTE REPORTED."
      ],
      "style": "emphasis",
      "emphasisWords": [
        "NO VOTE REPORTED"
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 30.137,
      "end": 33.137,
      "kind": "lowerthird",
      "primary": "FIVE PAGES",
      "secondary": "Almost everything a person would want to know about these three families is not in them"
    },
    {
      "start": 43.626,
      "end": 49.626,
      "kind": "acttitle",
      "title": "THREE SUITS, TWO PAPERS",
      "kicker": "ACT ONE",
      "index": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 61.277,
      "end": 67.277,
      "kind": "compbars",
      "items": [
        {
          "label": "Plaintiffs",
          "value": 3
        },
        {
          "label": "Nursing homes",
          "value": 2
        },
        {
          "label": "States",
          "value": 1
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 78.928,
      "end": 84.928,
      "kind": "lowerthird",
      "primary": "25 AUGUST 2009",
      "secondary": "The Circuit Court of Kanawha County dismisses Clayton Brown's suit"
    },
    {
      "start": 96.579,
      "end": 102.579,
      "kind": "kinetic",
      "lines": [
        "THAT ORDER IS",
        "ONE PARAGRAPH LONG."
      ],
      "style": "emphasis",
      "emphasisWords": [
        "ONE PARAGRAPH"
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 114.229,
      "end": 120.229,
      "kind": "lowerthird",
      "primary": "29 SEPTEMBER 2009",
      "secondary": "The same court, five weeks later — Jeffrey Taylor's suit"
    },
    {
      "start": 131.88,
      "end": 137.88,
      "kind": "kinetic",
      "lines": [
        "SAME COURT.",
        "SAME TWO ARGUMENTS.",
        "SAME ANSWER."
      ],
      "style": "emphasis",
      "emphasisWords": [
        "SAME ANSWER"
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 149.531,
      "end": 155.531,
      "kind": "lowerthird",
      "primary": "2 JUNE 2010",
      "secondary": "The Circuit Court of Harrison County refuses to compel arbitration, and certifies a question upward"
    },
    {
      "start": 167.182,
      "end": 173.182,
      "kind": "arrow",
      "from": [
        0.26,
        0.68
      ],
      "to": [
        0.72,
        0.32
      ],
      "label": "Two dismissals and one question, all travelling to the Supreme Court of Appeals of West Virginia"
    },
    {
      "start": 184.832,
      "end": 190.832,
      "kind": "stat",
      "value": 2,
      "label": "Sentences the opinion gives to what happened to the three patients"
    },
    {
      "start": 202.483,
      "end": 208.483,
      "kind": "kinetic",
      "lines": [
        "NO AGES. NO DATES.",
        "NO DESCRIPTION",
        "OF THE CARE."
      ],
      "style": "emphasis",
      "emphasisWords": [
        "NO DESCRIPTION"
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 220.134,
      "end": 226.134,
      "kind": "lowerthird",
      "primary": "PAULINE VIRGINIA WILLETT",
      "secondary": "The only patient named anywhere in the opinion, and only in the caption of Marchio's case"
    },
    {
      "start": 237.785,
      "end": 243.785,
      "kind": "kinetic",
      "lines": [
        "THE SAME FOUR WORDS,",
        "TWICE.",
        "A FAMILY MEMBER."
      ],
      "style": "emphasis",
      "emphasisWords": [
        "A FAMILY MEMBER"
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 255.436,
      "end": 261.436,
      "kind": "quote",
      "quote": "The contracts included a clause requiring the parties to arbitrate all disputes, other than claims to collect late payments owed by the patient.",
      "attribution": "Marmet Health Care Center, Inc. v. Brown (2012) (per curiam), Part I"
    },
    {
      "start": 273.086,
      "end": 279.086,
      "kind": "lowerthird",
      "primary": "THE FILING FEE",
      "secondary": "The party filing the arbitration pays it, in accordance with the Rules of the American Arbitration Association fee schedules. The opinion states no dollar figure."
    },
    {
      "start": 290.737,
      "end": 296.737,
      "kind": "quote",
      "quote": "The agreement in Marchio's case also included a clause requiring arbitration but made no exceptions to the arbitration requirement and did not mention filing fees.",
      "attribution": "Marmet (2012) (per curiam), Part I"
    },
    {
      "start": 308.388,
      "end": 314.388,
      "kind": "quote",
      "quote": "Any waiver by a resident or his or her legal representative of the right to commence an action under this section, whether oral or in writing, shall be null and void as contrary to public policy.",
      "attribution": "West Virginia Nursing Home Act, W. Va. Code 16-5C-15(c) [1997], set out in Brown II (2012), n. 6"
    },
    {
      "start": 326.039,
      "end": 332.039,
      "kind": "numberticker",
      "value": 1925,
      "label": "The year of the Federal Arbitration Act, set against a state statute of 1997",
      "group": false
    },
    {
      "start": 355.357,
      "end": 361.357,
      "kind": "acttitle",
      "title": "BROWN ONE",
      "kicker": "ACT TWO",
      "index": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 377.342,
      "end": 383.342,
      "kind": "quote",
      "quote": "[a] state statute, rule, or common-law doctrine, which targets arbitration provisions for disfavored treatment and which is not usually applied to other types of contract provisions, stands as an obstacle to the accomplishment and execution of the purposes and objectives of the Federal Arbitration Act ... and is preempted.",
      "attribution": "Brown I (2011), Syllabus Point 8, quoted in Brown II (2012), n. 12"
    },
    {
      "start": 399.328,
      "end": 405.328,
      "kind": "lowerthird",
      "primary": "SYLLABUS POINT 11",
      "secondary": "Section 15(c), to the extent it voids arbitration clauses in nursing home contracts, is preempted by the Federal Arbitration Act"
    },
    {
      "start": 421.314,
      "end": 427.314,
      "kind": "kinetic",
      "lines": [
        "ON THE STATUTE,",
        "WEST VIRGINIA AGREED",
        "WITH THE NURSING HOMES."
      ],
      "style": "emphasis",
      "emphasisWords": [
        "AGREED"
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 443.299,
      "end": 449.299,
      "kind": "lowerthird",
      "primary": "SYLLABUS POINT 21",
      "secondary": "The holding that travelled to Washington"
    },
    {
      "start": 465.285,
      "end": 471.285,
      "kind": "kinetic",
      "lines": [
        "THE LOAD IS ON",
        "ONE WORD.",
        "PRIOR."
      ],
      "style": "emphasis",
      "emphasisWords": [
        "PRIOR"
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 487.27,
      "end": 493.27,
      "kind": "quote",
      "quote": "as a matter of public policy under West Virginia law, an arbitration clause in a nursing home admission agreement adopted prior to an occurrence of negligence that results in a personal injury or wrongful death, shall not be enforced to compel arbitration of a dispute concerning the negligence.",
      "attribution": "The Supreme Court of Appeals of West Virginia, quoted in Marmet (2012), Part I (Pet. App. 85a–86a)"
    },
    {
      "start": 509.256,
      "end": 515.256,
      "kind": "kinetic",
      "lines": [
        "TWO WERE CALLED",
        "UNCONSCIONABLE.",
        "THE THIRD WAS",
        "A CERTIFIED QUESTION."
      ],
      "style": "emphasis",
      "emphasisWords": [
        "UNCONSCIONABLE"
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 531.241,
      "end": 537.241,
      "kind": "kinetic",
      "lines": [
        "TWO SEPARATE DOORS.",
        "ONE CATEGORY.",
        "ONE CONTRACT."
      ],
      "style": "emphasis",
      "emphasisWords": [
        "TWO SEPARATE DOORS"
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 553.227,
      "end": 559.227,
      "kind": "lowerthird",
      "primary": "ADMISSION DAY",
      "secondary": "'often fraught with urgency, confusion, and stress' — Brown I, quoted in Brown II, n. 20"
    },
    {
      "start": 575.213,
      "end": 581.213,
      "kind": "quote",
      "quote": "People seek medical care in a nursing home for long-term treatment to heal, and do so only a few times in life. Nursing homes daily sign contracts with patients as a routine course of doing business.",
      "attribution": "Brown II (2012) — the state court's own sentences, written after the remand"
    },
    {
      "start": 597.198,
      "end": 603.198,
      "kind": "quote",
      "quote": "The doctrine of unconscionability means that, because of an overall and gross imbalance, one-sidedness or lop-sidedness in a contract, a court may be justified in refusing to enforce the contract as written.",
      "attribution": "Brown I, Syllabus Point 12, quoted in Brown II (2012), n. 22"
    },
    {
      "start": 619.184,
      "end": 625.184,
      "kind": "quote",
      "quote": "the courts of this State are not hostile to arbitration or to adhesion contracts. We are hostile toward contracts of adhesion that are unconscionable and rely upon arbitration as an artifice to defraud a weaker party of rights clearly provided by the common law or statute.",
      "attribution": "The Supreme Court of Appeals of West Virginia, quoted in Brown II (2012), n. 19"
    },
    {
      "start": 641.169,
      "end": 647.169,
      "kind": "quote",
      "quote": "A contract of adhesion is one drafted and imposed by a party of superior strength that leaves the subscribing party little or no opportunity to alter the substantive terms, and only the opportunity to adhere to the contract or reject it.",
      "attribution": "Brown I, Syllabus Point 18, quoted in Brown II (2012), n. 35"
    },
    {
      "start": 663.155,
      "end": 669.155,
      "kind": "quote",
      "quote": "[f]inding that there is an adhesion contract is the beginning point for analysis, not the end of it; what courts aim at doing is distinguishing good adhesion contracts which should be enforced from bad adhesion contracts which should not.",
      "attribution": "State ex rel. Dunlap v. Berger (2002), quoted in Brown II (2012), n. 36"
    },
    {
      "start": 685.141,
      "end": 691.141,
      "kind": "quote",
      "quote": "It may be disingenuous for a nursing home to later assert that the patient or family member consciously, knowingly and deliberately accepted an arbitration clause in the contract, and understood the clause was intended to eliminate their access to the courts if the nursing home negligently injured or killed the patient.",
      "attribution": "Brown II (2012) — the state court's own sentence"
    },
    {
      "start": 707.126,
      "end": 713.126,
      "kind": "lowerthird",
      "primary": "11-391 · 11-394",
      "secondary": "Two petitions for certiorari. The defendants specifically challenged Syllabus Point 21."
    },
    {
      "start": 737.999,
      "end": 743.999,
      "kind": "acttitle",
      "title": "WHOLE CLOTH",
      "kicker": "ACT THREE",
      "index": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 758.76,
      "end": 764.76,
      "kind": "quote",
      "quote": "With tendentious reasoning, the United States Supreme Court has stretched the application of the FAA from being a procedural statutory scheme effective only in the federal courts, to being a substantive law that preempts state law in both the federal and state courts.",
      "attribution": "Brown I (2011), quoted in Brown II (2012), n. 14"
    },
    {
      "start": 779.52,
      "end": 785.52,
      "kind": "lowerthird",
      "primary": "THE FEDERAL ARBITRATION ACT, 1925",
      "secondary": "The state court read the text and the congressional history as a scheme for commercial entities engaged in interstate commerce"
    },
    {
      "start": 800.28,
      "end": 806.28,
      "kind": "kinetic",
      "lines": [
        "COMMERCIAL ENTITIES.",
        "NATIONWIDE ENFORCEMENT."
      ],
      "style": "emphasis",
      "emphasisWords": [
        "COMMERCIAL ENTITIES"
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 821.041,
      "end": 827.041,
      "kind": "kinetic",
      "lines": [
        "A PANACEA",
        "FOR ALL THE WOES",
        "OF LITIGATION."
      ],
      "style": "emphasis",
      "emphasisWords": [
        "A PANACEA"
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 841.801,
      "end": 847.801,
      "kind": "quote",
      "quote": "Congress did not intend for the FAA to be, in any way, applicable to personal injury or wrongful death suits that only collaterally derive from a written agreement that evidences a transaction affecting interstate commerce",
      "attribution": "The Supreme Court of Appeals of West Virginia, quoted in Marmet (2012), Part I (Pet. App. 84a)"
    },
    {
      "start": 862.562,
      "end": 868.562,
      "kind": "quote",
      "quote": "State and federal courts must enforce the Federal Arbitration Act (FAA), 9 U. S. C. §1 et seq., with respect to all arbitration agreements covered by that statute.",
      "attribution": "Marmet Health Care Center, Inc. v. Brown (2012) (per curiam) — the opinion's first sentence"
    },
    {
      "start": 883.322,
      "end": 889.322,
      "kind": "kinetic",
      "lines": [
        "MISREADING.",
        "DISREGARDING.",
        "ONE IS ERROR.",
        "THE OTHER IS CHOICE."
      ],
      "style": "emphasis",
      "emphasisWords": [
        "THE OTHER IS CHOICE"
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 904.082,
      "end": 910.082,
      "kind": "quote",
      "quote": "The state court held unenforceable all predispute arbitration agreements that apply to claims alleging personal injury or wrongful death against nursing homes.",
      "attribution": "Marmet (2012) (per curiam), opening paragraph"
    },
    {
      "start": 924.843,
      "end": 930.843,
      "kind": "quote",
      "quote": "written provision in . . . a contract evidencing a transaction involving commerce to settle by arbitration a controversy thereafter arising out of such contract or transaction . . . shall be valid, irrevocable, and enforceable, save upon such grounds as exist at law or in equity for the revocation of any contract.",
      "attribution": "9 U. S. C. §2, quoted in Marmet (2012), Part I"
    },
    {
      "start": 945.603,
      "end": 951.603,
      "kind": "kinetic",
      "lines": [
        "KEEP THE SECOND HALF.",
        "IT COMES BACK."
      ],
      "style": "emphasis",
      "emphasisWords": [
        "SECOND HALF"
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 966.364,
      "end": 972.364,
      "kind": "kinetic",
      "lines": [
        "NO EXCEPTION",
        "FOR PERSONAL INJURY.",
        "NO EXCEPTION",
        "FOR WRONGFUL DEATH."
      ],
      "style": "emphasis",
      "emphasisWords": [
        "NO EXCEPTION"
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 987.124,
      "end": 993.124,
      "kind": "quote",
      "quote": "[w]hen state law prohibits outright the arbitration of a particular type of claim, the analysis is straightforward: The conflicting rule is displaced by the FAA.",
      "attribution": "AT&T Mobility LLC v. Concepcion (2011), quoted in Marmet (2012), Part I"
    },
    {
      "start": 1007.885,
      "end": 1013.885,
      "kind": "quote",
      "quote": "West Virginia's prohibition against predispute agreements to arbitrate personal-injury or wrongful-death claims against nursing homes is a categorical rule prohibiting arbitration of a particular type of claim, and that rule is contrary to the terms and coverage of the FAA.",
      "attribution": "Marmet (2012) (per curiam), Part I"
    },
    {
      "start": 1028.645,
      "end": 1034.645,
      "kind": "casetimeline_c",
      "events": [
        {
          "year": "1984",
          "text": "Southland v. Keating — pre-empted"
        },
        {
          "year": "1987",
          "text": "Perry v. Thomas — pre-empted"
        },
        {
          "year": "1995",
          "text": "Mastrobuono — pre-empted"
        },
        {
          "year": "2008",
          "text": "Preston v. Ferrer — pre-empted"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 1049.405,
      "end": 1055.405,
      "kind": "quote",
      "quote": "The West Virginia court's interpretation of the FAA was both incorrect and inconsistent with clear instruction in the precedents of this Court.",
      "attribution": "Marmet (2012) (per curiam), Part I"
    },
    {
      "start": 1070.166,
      "end": 1076.166,
      "kind": "quote",
      "quote": "When this Court has fulfilled its duty to interpret federal law, a state court may not contradict or fail to implement the rule so established.",
      "attribution": "Marmet (2012) (per curiam), citing U. S. Const., Art. VI, cl. 2"
    },
    {
      "start": 1098.136,
      "end": 1104.136,
      "kind": "acttitle",
      "title": "PART TWO",
      "kicker": "ACT FOUR",
      "index": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 1114.317,
      "end": 1120.317,
      "kind": "quote",
      "quote": "The West Virginia court proposed an 'alternativ[e]' holding that the particular arbitration clauses in Brown's case and Taylor's case were unconscionable.",
      "attribution": "Marmet (2012) (per curiam), Part II"
    },
    {
      "start": 1130.497,
      "end": 1136.497,
      "kind": "compbars",
      "items": [
        {
          "label": "Brown and Taylor: condemned twice",
          "value": 2
        },
        {
          "label": "Marchio: condemned once, on the categorical rule alone",
          "value": 1
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 1146.678,
      "end": 1152.678,
      "kind": "quote",
      "quote": "It is unclear, however, to what degree the state court's alternative holding was influenced by the invalid, categorical rule discussed above, the rule against predispute arbitration agreements.",
      "attribution": "Marmet (2012) (per curiam), Part II"
    },
    {
      "start": 1162.859,
      "end": 1168.859,
      "kind": "highlightring",
      "cx": 0.48,
      "cy": 0.54,
      "r": 0.14,
      "label": "clearly violates public policy — found inside the contract analysis"
    },
    {
      "start": 1179.039,
      "end": 1185.039,
      "kind": "quote",
      "quote": "On remand, the West Virginia court must consider whether, absent that general public policy, the arbitration clauses in Brown's case and Taylor's case are unenforceable under state common law principles that are not specific to arbitration and pre-empted by the FAA.",
      "attribution": "Marmet (2012) (per curiam), Part II — the whole of what was sent back"
    },
    {
      "start": 1195.22,
      "end": 1201.22,
      "kind": "kinetic",
      "lines": [
        "THE LAST CLAUSE",
        "IS THE SAVINGS CLAUSE.",
        "SECTION 2, BACK AGAIN."
      ],
      "style": "emphasis",
      "emphasisWords": [
        "SAVINGS CLAUSE"
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 1211.4,
      "end": 1217.4,
      "kind": "compbars",
      "items": [
        {
          "label": "A rule that says this type of claim does not go to arbitration",
          "value": 0
        },
        {
          "label": "A ground that exists for the revocation of any contract",
          "value": 1
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 1227.581,
      "end": 1233.581,
      "kind": "quote",
      "quote": "The petition for certiorari is granted. The judgment of the Supreme Court of Appeals of West Virginia is vacated, and the cases are remanded for proceedings not inconsistent with this opinion.",
      "attribution": "Marmet (2012) (per curiam), disposition"
    },
    {
      "start": 1243.762,
      "end": 1249.762,
      "kind": "kinetic",
      "lines": [
        "IT DID NOT HOLD",
        "THE CLAUSES VALID.",
        "IT DID NOT ORDER",
        "ANYONE TO ARBITRATE."
      ],
      "style": "emphasis",
      "emphasisWords": [
        "DID NOT"
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 1259.942,
      "end": 1265.942,
      "kind": "kinetic",
      "lines": [
        "ONE RULE FELL.",
        "EVERYTHING ELSE",
        "WENT BACK."
      ],
      "style": "emphasis",
      "emphasisWords": [
        "EVERYTHING ELSE"
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 1276.123,
      "end": 1282.123,
      "kind": "lowerthird",
      "primary": "THE QUESTION NOBODY REACHED",
      "secondary": "Whether a relative's signature on an admission form can bind a patient, or a patient's estate, at all. It is in the file. The five pages do not mention it."
    },
    {
      "start": 1292.303,
      "end": 1298.303,
      "kind": "kinetic",
      "lines": [
        "THAT CLAUSE WAS",
        "IN FRONT OF THE COURT.",
        "NOBODY CHALLENGED IT."
      ],
      "style": "emphasis",
      "emphasisWords": [
        "NOBODY CHALLENGED IT"
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 1308.484,
      "end": 1314.484,
      "kind": "lowerthird",
      "primary": "PER CURIAM",
      "secondary": "By the court. No author, no reported vote. Not a synonym for unanimous."
    },
    {
      "start": 1324.665,
      "end": 1330.665,
      "kind": "lowerthird",
      "primary": "3 APRIL 2012",
      "secondary": "The Supreme Court of Appeals of West Virginia orders additional briefs and arguments, and hears the cases again"
    },
    {
      "start": 1340.845,
      "end": 1346.845,
      "kind": "kinetic",
      "lines": [
        "ONE SIDE ASKED",
        "FOR DISCOVERY.",
        "THE OTHER SAID THE RECORD",
        "WAS ALREADY EMPTY."
      ],
      "style": "emphasis",
      "emphasisWords": [
        "ALREADY EMPTY"
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 1357.026,
      "end": 1363.026,
      "kind": "numberticker",
      "value": 7,
      "label": "Days from submission to opinion — submitted 6 June 2012, decided 13 June 2012",
      "group": false
    },
    {
      "start": 1385.733,
      "end": 1391.733,
      "kind": "acttitle",
      "title": "BROWN TWO",
      "kicker": "ACT FIVE",
      "index": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 1407.968,
      "end": 1413.968,
      "kind": "quote",
      "quote": "In accordance with the Supreme Court's mandate, we overrule Syllabus Point 21 of Brown I. We otherwise find that the Supreme Court's decision does not counsel us to alter our original analysis of West Virginia's common law of contracts.",
      "attribution": "Brown II, 229 W. Va. 382 (2012), Ketchum, C.J."
    },
    {
      "start": 1430.202,
      "end": 1436.202,
      "kind": "quote",
      "quote": "The Supreme Court's opinion did not discuss any other portion of Brown I, aside from Syllabus Point 21 and its accompanying text.",
      "attribution": "Brown II (2012)"
    },
    {
      "start": 1452.436,
      "end": 1458.436,
      "kind": "quote",
      "quote": "The parties have not challenged our holding in Syllabus Point 11 of Brown I regarding the preemption of Section 15(c) by Section 2 of the FAA, and we need not revisit it.",
      "attribution": "Brown II (2012)"
    },
    {
      "start": 1474.671,
      "end": 1480.671,
      "kind": "quote",
      "quote": "The doctrine of unconscionability that we explicated in Brown I is a general, state, common-law, contract-law principle that is not specific to arbitration, and does not implicate the FAA.",
      "attribution": "Brown II (2012)"
    },
    {
      "start": 1496.905,
      "end": 1502.905,
      "kind": "kinetic",
      "lines": [
        "SUMMARILY.",
        "WITHOUT ELUCIDATING",
        "HOW AND WHY."
      ],
      "style": "emphasis",
      "emphasisWords": [
        "SUMMARILY"
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 1519.14,
      "end": 1525.14,
      "kind": "kinetic",
      "lines": [
        "IT KEPT THE ADHESION ANALYSIS.",
        "IT KEPT THE SLIDING SCALE.",
        "IT KEPT THE WHOLE APPARATUS."
      ],
      "style": "emphasis",
      "emphasisWords": [
        "IT KEPT"
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 1541.374,
      "end": 1547.374,
      "kind": "quote",
      "quote": "A contract term is unenforceable if it is both procedurally and substantively unconscionable. However, both need not be present to the same degree.",
      "attribution": "Brown I, Syllabus Point 20, quoted in Brown II (2012), n. 32"
    },
    {
      "start": 1563.609,
      "end": 1569.609,
      "kind": "quote",
      "quote": "Agreements to arbitrate must contain at least 'a modicum of bilaterality' to avoid unconscionability.",
      "attribution": "Abramson v. Juniper Networks, quoted in Brown II (2012), n. 40"
    },
    {
      "start": 1585.843,
      "end": 1591.843,
      "kind": "quote",
      "quote": "claims of coercion, fraud, or unequal bargaining power in the formation of an arbitration agreement are 'best left for resolution in specific cases'",
      "attribution": "Brown II (2012), n. 49, quoting Gilmer v. Interstate/Johnson Lane Corp. (1991)"
    },
    {
      "start": 1608.077,
      "end": 1614.077,
      "kind": "quote",
      "quote": "The circuit court's order in Brown's case is devoid of any findings of fact or conclusions of law on the question of unconscionability.",
      "attribution": "Brown II (2012)"
    },
    {
      "start": 1630.312,
      "end": 1636.312,
      "kind": "quote",
      "quote": "We conclude the correct course is to remand these cases to the circuit courts for the taking of evidence, the full development of a record, and proper consideration of whether the clauses are unconscionable.",
      "attribution": "Brown II (2012)"
    },
    {
      "start": 1652.546,
      "end": 1658.546,
      "kind": "kinetic",
      "lines": [
        "TWO MORE ARGUMENTS.",
        "REFUSED —",
        "NOT ON THE MERITS."
      ],
      "style": "emphasis",
      "emphasisWords": [
        "NOT ON THE MERITS"
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 1674.781,
      "end": 1680.781,
      "kind": "lowerthird",
      "primary": "THE FORUMS NAMED IN THE PAPERS",
      "secondary": "Effective 1 January 2003, the American Arbitration Association announced it would no longer accept individual-patient cases without a post-dispute agreement to arbitrate; the National Arbitration Forum stopped administering consumer disputes as of 24 July 2009"
    },
    {
      "start": 1697.015,
      "end": 1703.015,
      "kind": "quote",
      "quote": "there is no evidence in the record that the family member who signed each admission agreement had the legal authority to sign an arbitration clause, and thereby waive the resident's or resident's heirs right to pursue action in court",
      "attribution": "Brown II (2012), n. 52 — the plaintiffs' second argument"
    },
    {
      "start": 1719.249,
      "end": 1725.249,
      "kind": "quote",
      "quote": "We decline to consider these two arguments, which should be considered by the trial court first.",
      "attribution": "Brown II (2012), n. 52"
    },
    {
      "start": 1741.484,
      "end": 1747.484,
      "kind": "casetimeline_c",
